"computed on a random subsample of {} values (plus the minimum and maximum) "
"rather than the full data, because the exact algorithm is too slow at this "
"size. The subsample is drawn with a fixed seed, so repeated runs give the "
"same break points, but they are an approximation to the optimum. Quantile "
"binning uses every observation if exact boundaries matter."
msgstr ""
